            <section class="spread t-hero-plus-stack"
             data-spread="location"
             data-dimension="place"><h2>geography</h2><div class="prose-slot" lang="en"><p>Paris is located in northern central France, in a north-bending arc of the river <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seine">Seine</a>, whose crest includes two islands, the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C3%8Ele_Saint-Louis">Île Saint-Louis</a> and the larger <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C3%8Ele_de_la_Cit%C3%A9">Île de la Cité</a>, which form the oldest part of Paris. The river's mouth on the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/English_Channel">English Channel</a> (<i>La Manche</i>) is about 233&#160;mi (375&#160;km) downstream from Paris. Paris is spread widely on both banks of the river. Overall, Paris is relatively flat, and the lowest point is 35&#160;m (115&#160;ft) <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Above_mean_sea_level">above sea level</a>. Paris has several prominent hills, the highest of which is <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Montmartre">Montmartre</a> at 130&#160;m (427&#160;ft).</p><a class="read" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paris#Geography">Geography ↗</a></div><div data-slot="hero">
