            <section class="spread t-axis"
             data-spread="history"
             data-dimension="time"><h2>history</h2><div class="prose-slot" lang="en"><p>The <i><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parisii_(Gaul)">Parisii</a></i> people inhabited the Paris area from around the middle of the 3rd century BC. One of the area's major north–south trade routes crossed the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seine">Seine</a> on the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C3%8Ele_de_la_Cit%C3%A9">Île de la Cité</a>, which gradually became an important trading centre. The Parisii traded with many river towns, some as far away as the Iberian Peninsula, and minted their own coins.</p><a class="read" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paris#History">History ↗</a></div><div data-slot="axis">
        <div class="axis">
    <div class="ends"><span>300 BCE</span><span>2024</span></div><div class="track">
